  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "1: Create the Single Page Application in Your Auth0 Tenant",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "Create the SPA in Auth0",
      "description": "## Create the SPA in Auth0\nBefore you can begin configuring the Single Page Application for authentication, it must be registered in the Auth0 dashboard. Let's do that now.\n\n1. From your Auth0 Dashboard, make sure you have your **dev-** tenant selected.\n\n1. Go to **Applications** > **Applications**.\n\n1. Create a new application with the following attributes:\n    - **Name**: Lab: SPA\n    - **Application type**: Single Page Web Application\n    > Note: Your lab MUST be named exactly **Lab: SPA**.\n\n1. Once you have created the new application integration, select the **Settings** tab.\n1. Scroll down to the **Allowed Callback URLs** and copy and paste the value that prints out when you select [this link](command:codetour.sendTextToTerminal?[\"echo https://$CODESPACE_NAME-3000.app.github.dev\"]). This is your app's URL served through this Codespace.\n1. Paste the same value into the **Allowed Logout URLs** field.\n1. **Save** your changes.\n\n>Note: You can also find your app's Codespace URL by going to the **PORTS** tab in the Codespace. It's under **Forwarded Address** for port 38500."
    },
    {
      "file": "",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "Configure this Lab",
      "description": "## Configure this Lab\nNow, you'll use a command to the Auth0 extension for VSCode that will reach out to your tenant through the CLI and ensure that it is configured appropriately for this lab. \n\n1. Select [this link](command:auth0.lab.tenantConfigure) to ensure your lab tenant is properly configured. (Note: This will register an API called Lab: API with your tenant).\n\n    Wait until you see the message that `resources.xml` has been successfully deploy before continuing to the next step.\n    \n    ![resources deployed message](https://cdn.auth0.com/website/a0fun/v2/resources.png)\n\n1. Select [this link](command:auth0.lab.localConfigure) to set your local environment configurations (creates `.env` files in `/spa-app` and `/api`).\n\n> Note: If you do not see the .env files generated, check the following:\n> - You are logged into the correct tenant on the Auth0 Extension.\n> - You created a Single Page Application named exactly **Lab: SPA** on this tenant.\n> - You ran the command in item (1) to create the API, **Lab: API** on this tenant.\n\n> For additional troubleshooting see: https://auth0-training.github.io/#im-missing-an-env-file-for-my-application--my-application-doesnt-launch",
      "selection": {
        "start": {
          "line": 10,
          "character": 103
        },
        "end": {
          "line": 10,
          "character": 149
        }
      }
